      "hints": [
        "The original started from an inbound webhook (POST /test_voice_message_elevenlabs). Run it with `cdecli workflow run <slug> --ver <version> -d '{\"body\": {...}}'` or through the workflow API.",
        "\"Create collection\" authenticated with httpHeaderAuth in the original; add the matching Authorization header (or use the service's connector).",
        "\"Refresh collection\" authenticated with httpHeaderAuth in the original; add the matching Authorization header (or use the service's connector).",
        "\"AI Agent\" kept conversation memory (memoryBufferWindow); sessionId is set to the run-input sessionId.",
        "\"AI Agent\" used agent tools in the original: Vector Store Tool (toolVectorStore). The cdecli agent calls connectors directly; connect credentials for the services those tools reached.",
        "\"Qdrant Vector Store1\" folded a document (documentDefaultDataLoader); retrieved text is expected on the upstream payload as context/documents.",
        "\"Qdrant Vector Store1\" (vectorStoreQdrant.insert): The original used a Qdrant collection; here the default vector store is a Pinecone index with integrated embedding (upsert records), so Pinecone embeds the text itself.",
        "\"Qdrant Vector Store1\": create a Pinecone index with integrated embedding (for example llama-text-embed-v2, field map text=text) and set pineconeIndexHost; the Qdrant collection became the namespace \"{{pineconeNamespace}}\".",
        "Select the Project and Environment on the Workflow Configs node (the ids from `cdecli auth status`), then connect a credential for each connector below.",
        "Connect googlesuper: `cdecli credential create -n \"googlesuper\" -p googlesuper --template <formId> --secret <key>=<value>` (see `cdecli credential templates`).",
        "Connect pinecone: `cdecli credential create -n \"pinecone\" -p pinecone --template <formId> --secret <key>=<value>` (see `cdecli credential templates`)."
      ]
    },
    "notes": [
      "# STEP 4\n\n## RAG System\n\nClick on \"test workflow\" on n8n and \"Test AI agent\" on ElevenLabs. If everything is configured correctly, when you ask a question to the agent, the webhook on n8n is activated with the \"question\" field in the body filled with the question asked to the voice agent.\n\nThe AI ​​Agent will extract the information from the vector database, send it to the model to create the response which will be sent via the response webhook to ElevenLabs which will transform it into voice",
      "# STEP 1\n\n## Create an Agent on ElevenLabs \n- Create an agent on ElevenLabs (eg. test_n8n)\n- Add \"First message\" (eg. Hi, Can I help you?)\n- Add the \"System Prompt\" message... eg:\n'You are the waiter of \"Pizzeria da Michele\" in Verona. If you are asked a question, use the tool \"test_chatbot_elevenlabs\". When you receive the answer from \"test_chatbot_elevenlabs\" answer the user clearly and precisely.'\n- In Tools add a Webhook called eg. \"test_chatbot_elevenlabs\" and add the following description:\n'You are the waiter. Answer the questions asked and store them in the question field.'\n- Add the n8n webhook URL (method POST)\n- Enable \"Body Parameters\" and insert in the description \"Ask the user the question to ask the place.\", then in the \"Properties\" add a data type string called \"question\", value type \"LLM Prompt\" and description \"user question\"",
      "# STEP 2\n\n## Create Qdrant Collection\nChange:\n- QDRANTURL\n- COLLECTION",
      "# STEP 3\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n## Documents vectorization with Qdrant and Google Drive\nChange:\n- QDRANTURL\n- COLLECTION",
      "# STEP 5\n\n## Add Widget\n\nAdd the widget to your business website by replacing AGENT_ID with the agent id you created on ElevenLabs\n\n<elevenlabs-convai agent-id=\"AGENT_ID\"></elevenlabs-convai><script src=\"https://elevenlabs.io/convai-widget/index.js\" async type=\"text/javascript\"></script>"
    ],
